{
  "number": 1206,
  "title": "[FEATURE] Support for Bedrock Service Tiers",
  "url": "https://github.com/strands-agents/harness-sdk/issues/1206",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2025-11-19T14:47:24Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-04-02T21:01:05Z",
  "body": "### Problem Statement\n\nI would like Strands to support the newly introduced Service Tiers on Amazon Bedrock. https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-amazon-bedrock-service-tiers-help-you-match-ai-workload-performance-with-cost/ \n\n### Proposed Solution\n\nI'd like an optional field when creating an agent \"service-tier\" when using Bedrock models. There are three expected values: \"priority\", \"standard\", \"flex\". When the model does not support the service-tier, it will be gracefully handled with an warning message and won't be blocking. \n\n### Use Case\n\nThis would help lower the price for long workflows that are not time sensitive. \n\n### Alternatives Solutions\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional Context\n\n_No response_",
  "labels": [
    "enhancement",
    "ready for contribution",
    "area-model"
  ],
